You are debugging a production issue where a dynamic plugin framework in a Spring-based application continuously throws `java.lang.OutOfMemoryError: Metaspace` after repeated loading and unloading of plugin modules. You inspect the plugin loader implementation:

java
@Component
public class PluginLoader {
    private final Map<String, ClassLoader> activeLoaders = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    public void loadAndRegister(String pluginId, URL jarUrl) throws Exception {
        URLClassLoader childLoader = new URLClassLoader(new URL[]{jarUrl}, this.getClass().getClassLoader());
        Class<?> clazz = childLoader.loadClass("com.example.PluginEntry");
        Object pluginInstance = clazz.getDeclaredConstructor().newInstance();

        // Global registry holds instance reference for routing
        GlobalRegistry.registerPlugin(pluginId, pluginInstance);
        activeLoaders.put(pluginId, childLoader);
    }

    public void unload(String pluginId) {
        activeLoaders.remove(pluginId);
        // Custom cleanup logic executed here
    }
}

